WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.727
A blockchain is open, and a lot can be counted:

2
00:00:03.727 --> 00:00:07.247
transfers, addresses, fees, inflows to exchanges.

3
00:00:07.247 --> 00:00:09.259
But openness is not honesty.

4
00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:13.498
Address counts are inflated with millions of empty wallets,

5
00:00:13.498 --> 00:00:17.234
volume by sending the same coins around in a circle.

6
00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:20.682
What is harder to fake is what costs real money:

7
00:00:20.682 --> 00:00:22.694
fees, revenue, burned coins.

8
00:00:23.694 --> 00:00:24.551
The conclusion.

9
00:00:24.551 --> 00:00:29.293
Fundamental data answers the question of what this is and what it might be worth in

10
00:00:29.293 --> 00:00:29.635
years.

11
00:00:29.635 --> 00:00:33.120
But it is poorly suited to deciding whether to buy this week.

12
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.062
And the numbers worth trusting are those someone pays real money for.

13
00:00:38.062 --> 00:00:39.018
The main points.

14
00:00:39.018 --> 00:00:43.796
What matters is whether there is a path from the protocol's revenue to the token

15
00:00:43.796 --> 00:00:44.215
holder.

16
00:00:44.215 --> 00:00:46.723
Issuance and unlocks are constant sellers.

17
00:00:46.723 --> 00:00:51.502
And network activity and the coin's price are weakly linked and with a long lag.
